        <section id="api-json" class="api-card">
          <h2>Catalog API endpoints</h2>
          <p>
            Use these catalog endpoints for search, records, and facets.
            The <code>format</code> query parameter is the most reliable option when IDs include dots
            (for example <code>oocihm.N_00591</code>).
          </p>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><strong>Search endpoint:</strong> <code>GET /catalog?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code></li>
            <li><strong>Single record endpoint:</strong> <code>GET /catalog/:id?format=json</code></li>
            <li><strong>Facet endpoint:</strong> <code>GET /catalog/facet/:facet_id?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code></li>
            <li><strong>Single record export endpoint:</strong> <code>GET /catalog/:id?format=marc|marcxml|xml</code></li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="api-formats">Catalog response formats</h3>
          <p>
            Search requests currently return a JSON:API-style payload with top-level
            <code>links</code>, <code>meta</code>, <code>data</code>, and <code>included</code>.
          </p>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><strong>Search formats:</strong> <code>html</code>, <code>json</code></li>
            <li><strong>Single record formats:</strong> <code>html</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>marc</code>, <code>marcxml</code>, <code>xml</code></li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="api-params">Catalog query parameters</h3>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><code>q</code>: search query text (empty string returns the default result set)</li>
            <li><code>search_field</code>: one of <code>all_fields</code>, <code>full_title_tsim</code>, <code>author_tsim</code>, <code>subject_tsim</code>, <code>tx_gen</code></li>
            <li><code>lang</code>: response locale (<code>en</code> or <code>fr</code>)</li>
            <li><code>page</code>: result page number (starts at <code>1</code>)</li>
            <li><code>per_page</code>: page size (<code>10</code>, <code>20</code>, <code>50</code>, <code>100</code>)</li>
            <li><code>sort</code>: sort key (for example <code>date-added-desc</code>)</li>
            <li><code>f[field_name][]=value</code>: facet filters, for example <code>f[language_ssim_str][]=English</code></li>
            <li><code>range[pub_date_ssim][begin]</code> and <code>range[pub_date_ssim][end]</code>: year range filtering</li>
            <li><code>format</code>: output format (for example <code>json</code>)</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="api-config">Catalog configured fields, facets, and sorts</h3>
          <p><strong>Search fields:</strong> <code>all_fields</code>, <code>full_title_tsim</code>, <code>author_tsim</code>, <code>subject_tsim</code>, <code>tx_gen</code></p>
          <p><strong>Sort values:</strong> <code>relevance</code>, <code>year-desc</code>, <code>year-asc</code>, <code>date-added-desc</code>, <code>date-added-asc</code></p>
          <p><strong>Facet IDs:</strong> <code>pub_date_ssim</code>, <code>language_ssim_str</code>, <code>depositor_tsim_str</code>, <code>subject_ssim_str</code>, <code>author_ssm_str</code>, <code>collectionen_path</code>, <code>collectionfr_path</code>, <code>serial_title_str</code>, <code>is_issue_str</code>, <code>is_serial_str</code></p>
          <h3 id="api-structure">Catalog response structure</h3>
          <p>
            A search request such as
            <code>/catalog?search_field=all_fields&amp;q=&amp;format=json</code>
            returns:
          </p>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><code>links</code>: navigation URLs (<code>self</code>, <code>next</code>, <code>last</code>)</li>
            <li><code>meta.pages</code>: page state and counts (<code>current_page</code>, <code>total_pages</code>, <code>limit_value</code>, <code>total_count</code>)</li>
            <li><code>data[]</code>: search result records with <code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>attributes</code>, and <code>links.self</code></li>
            <li><code>included[]</code>: reusable API objects for facet definitions, search fields, and sort options</li>
          </ul>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Catalog response structure in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">JSON</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>{
    "links": {"self": "...", "next": "...", "last": "..."},
    "meta": {
        "pages": {
            "current_page": 1,
            "total_pages": 246,
            "limit_value": 10,
            "total_count": 2454
        }
    },
    "data": [
        {
            "id": "oocihm.N_00591",
            "type": "Newspaper",
            "attributes": {
                "title": "Keneder adler",
                "published_ssm": {
                    "type": "document_value",
                    "attributes": {"label": "Published", "value": "..."}
                },
                "language_ssim": {
                    "type": "document_value",
                    "attributes": {"label": "Language", "value": "..."}
                }
            },
            "links": {"self": "http://localhost:3000/catalog/oocihm.N_00591?lang=en"}
        }
    ],
    "included": [
        {"type": "facet", "id": "language_ssim_str"},
        {"type": "search_field", "id": "all_fields"},
        {"type": "sort", "id": "date-added-desc"}
    ]
}</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <p>
            Many <code>attributes.*.attributes.value</code> values are HTML fragments for display.
            If you are building a pure data pipeline, plan to strip or sanitize markup.
          </p>
