        <section id="api-iiif-query" class="api-card">
          <h2>IIIF API</h2>
          <p>
            The example below is based on manifest <code>m2025000007606h</code>
            (collection <code>69429</code>). It is a IIIF Presentation 3 manifest with
            <code>842</code> canvases.
          </p>
          <h3 id="iiif-endpoints">IIIF API endpoints</h3>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><strong>Get the ARK from catalog metadata:</strong> search JSON uses <code>data[i].attributes.ark.attributes.value</code>; single-record JSON uses <code>data.attributes.ark.attributes.value</code>. Extract the <code>href</code> URL from this HTML value (for example <code>https://n2t.net/ark:/69429/m2025000007606h</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Build the IIIF path from ARK:</strong> remove <code>https://n2t.net/ark:/</code> (or <code>ark:/</code>) to get <code>69429/m2025000007606h</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Manifest endpoint:</strong> <code>GET {presentation_service}/69429/m2025000007606h</code></li>
            <li><strong>Image info endpoint:</strong> <code>GET {image_service}/info.json</code></li>
            <li><strong>Image render endpoint:</strong> <code>GET {image_service}/{region}/{size}/{rotation}/{quality}.{format}</code></li>
            <li><strong>Content Search endpoint:</strong> <code>GET {content_search_service}/69429/m2025000007606h?q=canada</code></li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Full specification:
            <a href="https://iiif.io/api/image/2.1/">IIIF Image API 2.1</a>.
          </p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF Image API URL template in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests


def iiif_image_url(service_id, region="full", size="full", rotation="0", quality="default", fmt="jpg"):
    return f"{service_id}/{region}/{size}/{rotation}/{quality}.{fmt}"


service_id = "https://image-tor.canadiana.ca/iiif/2/69429%2Fc2025000026xr85"
image_url = iiif_image_url(service_id, region="full", size="500,")

response = requests.get(image_url, timeout=30)
response.raise_for_status()
print(response.headers["Content-Type"])  # image/jpeg</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><code>region</code>: <code>full</code>, <code>x,y,w,h</code>, or <code>pct:x,y,w,h</code></li>
            <li><code>size</code>: <code>full</code>, <code>w,</code>, <code>,h</code>, <code>w,h</code>, or <code>pct:n</code></li>
            <li><code>rotation</code>: <code>0</code>, <code>90</code>, <code>180</code>, <code>270</code> (and arbitrary angles if supported)</li>
            <li><code>quality</code>: service-dependent; this image supports <code>default</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>gray</code>, <code>bitonal</code></li>
            <li><code>format</code>: service-dependent; this image service advertises <code>jpg</code></li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="iiif-formats">IIIF response formats</h3>
          <ul class="api-list">
            <li><strong>Manifest endpoint:</strong> JSON (IIIF Presentation 3)</li>
            <li><strong>Image info endpoint (<code>info.json</code>):</strong> JSON (IIIF Image API)</li>
            <li><strong>Image render endpoint:</strong> binary image bytes (for example <code>image/jpeg</code>)</li>
            <li><strong>Content Search endpoint:</strong> JSON; <code>items</code> may be empty when there is no OCR match</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Manifest response shape (Presentation 3)</h3>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Manifest response shape in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">JSON</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>{
    "@context": "http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json",
    "id": "{presentation_service}/69429/m2025000007606h",
    "type": "Manifest",
    "label": {"en": ["Census returns for the 1901 Canadian census"]},
    "metadata": [
        {
            "label": {"en": ["Slug"]},
            "value": {"en": ["oocihm.lac_reel_t6428"]}
        }
    ],
    "summary": {"en": ["..."]},
    "items": [
        {
            "id": "{presentation_service}/canvas/69429/c2025000026xr85",
            "type": "Canvas",
            "width": 3936,
            "height": 3200,
            "label": {"en": ["Image 1"]},
            "items": [
                {
                    "type": "AnnotationPage",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "type": "Annotation",
                            "motivation": "painting",
                            "target": "{presentation_service}/canvas/69429/c2025000026xr85",
                            "body": {
                                "id": "{image_service}/full/max/0/default.jpg",
                                "type": "Image",
                                "format": "image/jpeg",
                                "width": 3936,
                                "height": 3200,
                                "service": [
                                    {
                                        "id": "{image_service}",
                                        "type": "ImageService2",
                                        "profile": "level2"
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "thumbnail": [{"id": "{image_service}/full/200,/0/default.jpg", "type": "Image", "format": "image/jpeg"}]
        }
	    ]
}</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h3>IIIF Image API response shape</h3>
          <p><code>info.json</code> returns JSON metadata:</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF info.json response in JSON">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Response</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">JSON</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>{
    "@context": "http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json",
    "@id": "{image_service}",
    "protocol": "http://iiif.io/api/image",
    "width": 3936,
    "height": 3200,
    "sizes": [{"width": 123, "height": 100}, "..."],
    "tiles": [{"width": 512, "height": 512, "scaleFactors": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]}],
    "profile": [
        "http://iiif.io/api/image/2/level1.json",
        {
            "formats": ["jpg"],
            "qualities": ["bitonal", "default", "gray", "color"],
            "supports": ["regionByPx", "sizeByW", "rotationBy90s", "..."]
        }
	    ]
}</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h3 id="iiif-examples">IIIF examples</h3>
          <h4>Example 1: ARK to manifest and content search</h4>
          <p>Extract ARK from catalog metadata, build IIIF path, fetch manifest, then run content search.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF workflow in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import re
import requests

BASE_URL = "http://localhost:3000"
PRESENTATION_SERVICE = "{presentation_service}"
CONTENT_SEARCH_SERVICE = "{content_search_service}"

# 1) Get a catalog record and extract ARK href from HTML value
record = requests.get(
    f"{BASE_URL}/catalog/oocihm.N_00591",
    params={"format": "json"},
    timeout=30,
).json()
ark_html = record["data"]["attributes"]["ark"]["attributes"]["value"]
ark_url = re.search(r'href="([^"]+)"', ark_html).group(1)

# 2) Normalize ARK path for IIIF services
ark_path = re.sub(r"^https?://n2t\\.net/ark:/?|^ark:/?", "", ark_url).lstrip("/")
# "69429/m2025000007606h"

# 3) Fetch manifest
manifest = requests.get(f"{PRESENTATION_SERVICE}/{ark_path}", timeout=30).json()
print(manifest["type"], len(manifest["items"]))  # Manifest 842

# 4) Derive image service from first canvas
image_service = manifest["items"][0]["items"][0]["items"][0]["body"]["service"][0]["id"]
info = requests.get(f"{image_service}/info.json", timeout=30).json()
print(info["width"], info["height"])

# 5) Run IIIF Content Search
search = requests.get(
    f"{CONTENT_SEARCH_SERVICE}/{ark_path}",
    params={"q": "canada"},
    timeout=30,
).json()
print(search["type"], len(search["items"]))</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h4>Example 2: IIIF image requests</h4>
          <p>Use the image service to inspect capabilities and request common derivatives.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="IIIF Image API requests in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>import requests

service_id = "https://image-tor.canadiana.ca/iiif/2/69429%2Fc2025000026xr85"

# Discover capabilities
info = requests.get(f"{service_id}/info.json", timeout=30).json()
print(info["width"], info["height"])  # 3936 3200

# Full image resized to width 500
img_small = requests.get(f"{service_id}/full/500,/0/default.jpg", timeout=30)
print(img_small.headers["Content-Type"])  # image/jpeg

# Crop by percent region, then resize
img_crop = requests.get(
    f"{service_id}/pct:25,25,50,50/800,/0/default.jpg",
    timeout=30,
)

# Rotated output
img_rotated = requests.get(f"{service_id}/full/500,/90/default.jpg", timeout=30)

# Alternate quality
img_gray = requests.get(f"{service_id}/full/500,/0/gray.jpg", timeout=30)</code></pre>
          </figure>
          <h4>Example 3: Binary image response</h4>
          <p>Read a rendered image response and verify MIME type before using raw bytes.</p>
          <figure class="api-snippet api-snippet--docmost" aria-label="Binary image response in Python">
            <figcaption>
              <span class="api-snippet__label">Code</span>
              <span class="api-snippet__lang">python</span>
            </figcaption>
            <pre class="api-code api-code--docmost"><code>response = requests.get(
    "https://image-tor.canadiana.ca/iiif/2/69429%2Fc2025000026xr85/full/500,/0/default.jpg",
    timeout=30,
)
response.raise_for_status()

print(response.headers["Content-Type"])  # image/jpeg
binary_jpeg = response.content            # bytes
print(len(binary_jpeg))</code></pre>
